<Shell title="Puri resort project" description="A locally rooted resort concept: open gardens, Odia village architecture and a practical investment kit in Odisha Investor." active="explore" wide related={false} shareImage={{src:'/assets/puri-resort/architecture-1280.webp',alt:'Puri resort concept with laterite cottages, tiled roofs and an open garden',width:1280,height:853}}>
<div class="wrap resort-project">
<nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Project Odisha</a></li><li><a href="/opportunities/">Tourism opportunities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Puri resort</li></ol></nav>
<header class="project-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Project Odisha · A concept to build upon</p><h1>A garden village.<br/><em>A sense of Puri.</em></h1><p class="lead">A resort where Odisha is present in the stone, the roofs, the trees and the spaces people share. This Puri concept brings that ambition into a practical starting point for entrepreneurs.</p><p class="status">Concept and planning stage · 26 October 2026</p><div class="actions"><a class="utk-button" href={kit}>Explore the investment kit</a><a class="utk-button utk-button--secondary" href={starter}>Start my own project</a></div></header>
<figure class="concept-image"><img src="/assets/puri-resort/architecture-1280.webp" srcset="/assets/puri-resort/architecture-640.webp 640w, /assets/puri-resort/architecture-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 800px) 92vw, 1100px" width="1280" height="853" fetchpriority="high" alt="Concept views of single-bedroom and family cottages, a two-storey courtyard building, and garden dining, with laterite stone and tiled roofs"/><figcaption>Architectural and landscape direction: cottage verandahs, an open courtyard and a garden shared by guests. These are concept illustrations, not construction drawings.</figcaption></figure>
<dl class="project-facts"><div><dt>Reference site</dt><dd>1.75 acres</dd></div><div><dt>Bookable units</dt><dd>36</dd></div><div><dt>Bedrooms</dt><dd>41</dd></div><div><dt>Starting point</dt><dd>Owned land</dd></div></dl>
<div class="reading">
<section><h2>Keep the place open.</h2><p>The brief starts with a rectangular plot, a north-facing entrance and a generous central park. Internal roads and paths should carry local craft and cultural details. Buildings and paths should make room for greenery and gathering, with a Tulasi chaura at the centre and Champa, Baula and Kadamba in the planting scheme.</p><p>The accommodation mix is 15 single-bedroom cottages, five two-bedroom family cottages and 16 units in a two-storey courtyard building. Each floor has eight units, with four on either side. That makes 36 booking units and 41 bedrooms.</p><p>The shared programme includes one swimming pool, recreation and children's play areas, gardens, a rain-dance area, an administration and community building with restaurants, and a 2,000 sq ft party hall.</p></section>
<section><h2>Let local materials shape the architecture.</h2><p>Mankada pathara is central to the brief, including the boundary wall. The ambition is to use local materials only, with tiled roofs, shaded verandahs and Pipili craft carrying Odisha's identity throughout the resort. Chilika and Konark provide themes for the landscape and common spaces.</p><p>The design should grow from local making and village life. Material origin, availability and suitability need to be established with suppliers, craftspeople and the architect before specifications are fixed.</p></section>
<section><h2>One project, two connected homes.</h2><p>Project Odisha shares the idea and its design principles so others can learn from them. Odisha Investor holds the working investment kit and the tools for adapting the idea into an entrepreneur's own project.</p><ul><li><strong>Read and explore:</strong> the illustrated concept, build-and-operate guide and source notes.</li><li><strong>Work through the numbers:</strong> editable worksheets for costs, cash flow, staffing, procurement and milestones.</li><li><strong>Make it your own:</strong> a separate workspace for your land details, cottage mix, material notes and six delivery stages.</li></ul><p>Starting a project creates a separate browser workspace and keeps existing drafts intact. A private cloud copy is saved only when you choose that action in Odisha Investor.</p><div class="actions"><a class="utk-button" href={kit}>Explore the investment kit</a><a class="utk-button utk-button--secondary" href={starter}>Start my own project</a></div></section>
<aside class="planning-limit"><h2>What must be established for a real site?</h2><p>This is a reusable concept, not an approved or operating resort. Exact plot dimensions, title, access, applicable approvals, water and power, a measured design and supplier quotations remain site-specific. The architect must establish whether the proposed mix fits while preserving the open space.</p><p>The kit contains legal and support research, financial examples and operating worksheets. Check its dated sources and replace the examples with site evidence before committing funds. No approval, subsidy sanction or investment return is represented as confirmed.</p></aside>
<section class="source"><h2>Project brief and working materials</h2><p>This overview follows Ahimanikya Satapathy's Puri resort brief and the <a href={kit}>Puri Resort Investment Kit, version 1.0</a>, dated 26 October 2026. Odisha Investor maintains the full guide, concept images, downloadable PDF and editable workbook together.</p><p><a href="/opportunities/">Return to tourism opportunities →</a></p></section>
</div></div>
